            "notes": "Round Two you are going to still be sticking to a more classic [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) and [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) build to keep earning currency.\n\nMy goal here is to have [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e) and [Mid-Air Mobilizer](item_760c1441-8cfa-426c-885d-8d0dec32e145) because of how significant of a power spike it is for Mercy. \n\nOn an ideal/good first round you should be able to afford both of these on top of your selected survival item of choice from R1.\n\nOn a less-ideal round it's alright to just go with just these two blues (and sell all your greens). If it comes down to having to pick one or the other, no stress, but focus [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e) first because of the uptime, and don't sell the greens.\n\nIf you are really finding survival difficult, you can exchange [Mid-Air Mobilizer](item_760c1441-8cfa-426c-885d-8d0dec32e145) for [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) from the Survival tab because it gives you 25 overhealth on every GA and can be clutch.",
