            "created_at": "2025-09-04T07:26:48.818515+00:00",
            "notes": "Round 3 is where the battle-Mercy part comes in.\n\nWhenever you have a few seconds charged from [Tethered Tourniquet](item_9ac02f9a-7c06-46a3-94d4-2ba9a9cf623f) and you see a good angle to pistol from, AND you have an ally in LOS to benefit from your beam, just start glocking. It's quite literally free real-estate.\n\nYou'll find with this combination of [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) and [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed), you will be doing an unexpected amount of damage, especially if you're hitting headshots. \n\nThe cool part about this build is that Mercy's ult-charge is built far, far more quickly by damage than by healing or damage boost (which is the slowest). So you want to be gaining Torniquet \"charge\" by healing OR damage-boosting (as it counts for both) and then getting as much damage out of your X seconds of free glock time as you can. \n\nIf you are in a Mercy mirror match up, you will be getting your Valkyrie significantly, significantly faster than the enemy Mercy if she is not using this build (and you're hitting your shots). You will also notice you will be getting more currency than her, because you are double-dipping in potential currency sources.\n\nThe best part is there is no downside to swapping to pistol as your beams will work as normal. Bonus: they work with the [Threads of Fate](item_cb61612b-9d83-49a9-989d-013bf084fbcb) extra beam target too!\n\nItem wise, you want to be picking [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power) Items that give you the most Power for your total income. Try to balance it at a 2:1 ratio of [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed) and [Weapon Power](stat_weapon_power). At this time the secondary effects of the items  do not matter: we are looking at numbers.",
